WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.345
Lesson 14.2.

00:00:02.345 --> 00:00:04.739
Automation: keepers, bots and agents

00:00:04.739 --> 00:00:06.980
without handing over the keys.

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:09.266
By the end of this lesson, you'll be able

00:00:09.266 --> 00:00:12.695
to automate routine actions with the least permission possible.

00:00:13.995 --> 00:00:15.285
Here's the plan.

00:00:15.285 --> 00:00:16.970
First, the key ideas.

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:19.685
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:19.685 --> 00:00:21.210
Then, your checklist.

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:23.372
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:24.672 --> 00:00:27.222
are met (e.g. repay when HF <

00:00:27.222 --> 00:00:30.752
1.8, rebalance an LP range). one thing

00:00:30.752 --> 00:00:34.047
(e.g. repay debt on one protocol, up to

00:00:34.047 --> 00:00:37.807
$X per day), revocable at any time. scoped

00:00:37.807 --> 00:00:41.776
rights, never your seed phrase or unlimited approvals. First,

00:00:41.776 --> 00:00:44.575
Keeper / automation networks execute pre-defined actions

00:00:44.575 --> 00:00:47.331
when conditions. Next, Smart-account permissions /

00:00:47.331 --> 00:00:50.119
session keys: grant a bot the

00:00:50.119 --> 00:00:52.371
right to do. Then, AI

00:00:52.371 --> 00:00:54.632
agents and bots: treat them like

00:00:54.632 --> 00:00:57.331
any other contract permission. They

00:00:57.331 --> 00:00:58.336
get. And

00:00:58.336 --> 00:01:00.760
finally, Test on a testnet or with

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:04.016
tiny amounts first; log every automated action.

00:01:05.317 --> 00:01:07.832
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:01:07.832 --> 00:01:11.685
Automated repay: a session key allowed only to call

00:01:11.685 --> 00:01:16.130
repay on your lending position, from your operating wallet,

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:19.542
capped at $5,000/day, expiring in 30 days.

00:01:19.542 --> 00:01:22.045
Worst case if the bot is compromised: it

00:01:22.045 --> 00:01:25.342
repays your debt, which is annoying, not catastrophic.

00:01:26.642 --> 00:01:28.102
Here's your checklist.

00:01:28.102 --> 00:01:29.637
Do it now, for real.

00:01:29.637 --> 00:01:34.012
First, each automation has a scoped, capped, expiring permission.

00:01:34.012 --> 00:01:38.792
Next, no automation holds seed phrases or unlimited approvals.

00:01:38.792 --> 00:01:43.137
And finally, Tested small; actions logged; revoke procedure known.

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:45.647
Question 1.

00:01:45.647 --> 00:01:46.777
What's a session key?

00:01:51.197 --> 00:01:53.277
The answer: A limited, revocable

00:01:53.277 --> 00:01:55.357
permission for a specific action.

00:01:56.657 --> 00:01:57.902
Question 2.

00:01:57.902 --> 00:02:00.597
Should an AI agent ever get your seed phrase?

00:02:05.017 --> 00:02:08.737
The answer: No. Give it scoped, revocable permissions only.

00:02:10.037 --> 00:02:11.307
Question 3.

00:02:11.307 --> 00:02:13.582
Worst case of a well-scoped repay bot?

00:02:18.002 --> 00:02:20.647
The answer: It repays debt within its cap.

00:02:20.647 --> 00:02:22.282
No funds leave your control.

00:02:23.582 --> 00:02:24.827
Let's recap.

00:02:24.827 --> 00:02:30.087
Keeper / automation networks execute pre-defined actions when conditions.

00:02:30.087 --> 00:02:32.737
Smart-account permissions / session keys.

00:02:32.737 --> 00:02:34.766
AI agents and bots: treat them

00:02:34.766 --> 00:02:37.357
like any other contract permission.

00:02:37.357 --> 00:02:40.102
Test on a testnet or with tiny amounts first.

00:02:41.402 --> 00:02:43.917
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:02:43.917 --> 00:02:47.497
Next up, Lesson 14.3: Operating procedures:

00:02:47.497 --> 00:02:50.914
multisig signing, change control, reviews.
